  "level": 1,
  "name": "Purchase requires an account",
  "note": "Draft: the purchase-session check includes bounded login-input and credential-tampering probes. The login probe replaces the password in one matched JSON form request with query-like text. Valid purchases must work before and after it. Stored order and stock reads must show no effect from a refused login or forgery. The read scope requires neither carts nor warehouses. Missing, ambiguous, repeated, redirected, non-JSON or incomplete login requests remain inconclusive. This proves one login string cannot grant purchase authority; it does not prove general injection safety. Unsupported or ambiguous credentials remain inconclusive, never a pass or an app defect. This does not test expiry or invalidation of previously copied tokens. After signout, the current browser credential must not authorize a purchase; sign-in must restore access. A bearer-only control must also succeed before cookies are omitted from the tampering probe. Cookie-only sessions still require one unambiguous cookie. Same-site and cross-site simple POSTs use the real browser cookie policy, without copied tokens. Complete opaque responses do not prove refusal: native state must remain unchanged, and valid purchases must still work. Local-network permission is granted only to the controlled origin because the appliance addresses are private.",
